-- title:
--   Divisibility of Igusa-branch functions by cₓ at a node
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` for which $q$ is a nonunit of $A$, an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ and an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$. Write $A_0 = A \cap k_0$ for the contraction of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and assume: $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, $A_0$ is henselian local, its residue field is algebraically closed, and every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some element of $k_0$ lying in $A$. Give `fieldBar q M'` (the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \subseteq$ `LaurentSeries` $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ attached to full level $q^2M'$) its $k_0$-algebra structure through $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Then let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ and $W_0$ a valuation subring of $F_0$ such that $W_0$ contracts to $A$ on $k_0$ (an $x \in k_0$ lies in $A$ iff its image lies in $W_0$), $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring, and the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates its maximal ideal. Let $O \subseteq F_0$ be a noetherian local subring with: $O \subseteq W_0$; $O$ contracts to $A$ on $k_0$; for each $f \in O$ there is $x \in k_0 \cap A$ with image in $O$ such that $f - x$ is a nonunit of $O$; and every $f \in F_0$ satisfies $fh = g$ for some $g, h \in O$ with $h \neq 0$. Fix $E_0 \geq 1$, assume the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $O$, and fix $c_x, c_y \in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the adic completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal onto `UVCrossingModel` of the adic completion $\widehat{A_0}$ of $A_0$ at the parameter $\pi^{E_0}$, $\pi$ the image of $\pi_0$, that is the quotient of `MvPowerSeries (Fin 2)` $\widehat{A_0}$ by `uvCrossingIdeal`, and units $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ of this quotient, subject to: $c_x c_y = \pi_0^{E_0} u$ in $O$; $\iota$ carries each constant coming from $k_0 \cap A$ to the corresponding `UVCrossingModel.const`; $\iota(c_x) = \gamma_U \cdot$ `UVCrossingModel.U` and $\iota(c_y) = \gamma_V \cdot$ `UVCrossingModel.V`. Finally let $W_x$ be a valuation subring of $F_0$ containing $O$, a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $\pi_0$, with $c_x$ in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ and $c_y$ outside it (these two conditions, and the hypothesis on $b$ below, being stated under the hypothesis of membership in $W_x$, which is automatic from $O \subseteq W_x$). The conclusion is that for every $b \in O$ lying in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ there exists a nonunit $m \in O$ with $b^{E_0+1} = c_x m$.
--
--   This is the local algebra at a node of the semistable model of the modular curve of full level: in the crossing presentation $\widehat{O} \cong \widehat{A_0}[[U,V]]/(UV - \pi_0^{E_0})$ the element $c_x$ cuts out the Igusa branch $W_x$, and the statement bounds how far a function vanishing along that branch can fail to be divisible by $c_x$, namely after raising to the power $E_0+1$. It is used in the construction of the unit separating the two branches at a node, [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_mem_eq_cx_mul_unit_isUnit_of_commonChart_of_igusaSep_of_prime`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_mem_eq_cx_mul_unit_isUnit_of_commonChart_of_igusaSep_of_prime).
